# API & Database Standards

## Response envelope (every endpoint, including errors)
```json
{ "data": { ... } | [ ... ] | null, "error": null }
{ "data": null, "error": { "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR", "message": "Invalid input", "details": [ { "field": "zip_code", "message": "ZIP must be 5 digits or ZIP+4" } ] } }
```
Error codes: `BAD_REQUEST`, `VALIDATION_ERROR`, `NOT_FOUND`, `INTERNAL_ERROR`.
Register global exception handlers so FastAPI's default error shapes never leak:
- `RequestValidationError`: malformed JSON (`json_invalid`) -> 400, field problems -> 422 with per-field details.
- Domain `NotFound` -> 404. Domain `ValidationFailed` -> 422. `DatabaseUnavailable` / unhandled -> 500 (generic message, full error in logs only).

## Endpoints
| Method | Path | Success | Errors | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| GET | /patients | 200 list | 400 bad filter | Filters: `last_name` (case-insensitive exact), `date_of_birth` (MM/DD/YYYY or YYYY-MM-DD), `phone_number` (normalized). Optional `limit` (default 50, max 200), `offset`. Excludes soft-deleted. Newest first |
| GET | /patients/{id} | 200 | 400 bad UUID, 404 missing or deleted | |
| POST | /patients | 201 created record incl. patient_id | 400, 422 | Ignores client-sent patient_id/created_at/updated_at/deleted_at |
| PUT | /patients/{id} | 200 updated record | 400 bad UUID or empty body, 404, 422 | Partial update: only fields present in the body change (`exclude_unset`). Setting an optional field to null clears it; required fields can't be null |
| DELETE | /patients/{id} | 200 with deleted record (or its id) | 400, 404 | Sets `deleted_at = now()`. Never hard delete. Deleting twice -> 404 |
| GET | /patients/{id}/calls | 200 list | 404 | Bonus: call logs/transcripts |
| GET | /health | 200 | 503 if DB down | DB ping + masked key pool status |

Output format: `date_of_birth` as MM/DD/YYYY (matches brief), timestamps as ISO 8601 UTC with `Z`.
Auto docs at `/docs` must stay accurate: add response models and examples.

## Validation & normalization (`app/core/validators.py`, reused by Pydantic schemas)
Normalize first (mode="before"), then validate. Strip whitespace, collapse internal spaces, reject control characters everywhere.
| Field | Normalize | Validate |
|---|---|---|
| first_name, last_name | trim, collapse spaces. Do NOT change case (McDonald, O'Neil) | 1-50 chars, regex `^[^\W\d_]+([ '\-][^\W\d_]+)*$` (unicode letters, single space/hyphen/apostrophe separators) |
| date_of_birth | accept MM/DD/YYYY and YYYY-MM-DD | real date, not after today (clinic timezone), not before 1900-01-01 |
| sex | case-insensitive; map M/F, "prefer not to say", "decline" | one of Male, Female, Other, Decline to Answer |
| phone_number, emergency_contact_phone | strip non-digits; drop leading 1 if 11 digits | exactly 10 digits, NANP: area code and exchange start with 2-9 |
| email | trim, lowercase | `email-validator` |
| address_line_1 | trim | 1-200 chars |
| address_line_2 | trim, empty -> null | max 100 |
| city | trim | 1-100 chars |
| state | uppercase; map full state names to codes ("texas" -> TX) | 50 states + DC + PR, GU, VI, AS, MP |
| zip_code | trim | `^\d{5}(-\d{4})?$` (accept 9 digits without dash and insert it) |
| insurance_member_id | uppercase, remove spaces and dashes | `^[A-Z0-9]{1,50}$` |
| preferred_language | trim, title case | default "English", max 50 |
| emergency_contact_name | trim | 1-100 chars, same char rules as names |

Document deliberate choices in README: spaces allowed in names (e.g. "De La Cruz"), state names accepted and normalized,
duplicate phone numbers allowed (family members can share a phone), so duplicates are handled conversationally not by a unique constraint.

## Database schema (`supabase/migrations/001_init.sql`, run in Supabase SQL editor)
```sql
create extension if not exists pgcrypto;

do $$ begin
  create type sex_type as enum ('Male', 'Female', 'Other', 'Decline to Answer');
exception when duplicate_object then null; end $$;

create table if not exists patients (
  patient_id              uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  first_name              varchar(50)  not null check (first_name ~ '^[[:alpha:]]+([ ''-][[:alpha:]]+)*$'),
  last_name               varchar(50)  not null check (last_name  ~ '^[[:alpha:]]+([ ''-][[:alpha:]]+)*$'),
  date_of_birth           date         not null check (date_of_birth >= date '1900-01-01' and date_of_birth <= current_date),
  sex                     sex_type     not null,
  phone_number            varchar(10)  not null check (phone_number ~ '^[2-9][0-9]{2}[2-9][0-9]{6}$'),
  email                   varchar(254) check (email is null or email ~* '^[^@[:space:]]+@[^@[:space:]]+\.[^@[:space:]]+$'),
  address_line_1          varchar(200) not null check (length(trim(address_line_1)) > 0),
  address_line_2          varchar(100),
  city                    varchar(100) not null check (length(trim(city)) > 0),
  state                   char(2)      not null check (state in (
    'AL','AK','AZ','AR','CA','CO','CT','DE','FL','GA','HI','ID','IL','IN','IA','KS','KY','LA','ME','MD',
    'MA','MI','MN','MS','MO','MT','NE','NV','NH','NJ','NM','NY','NC','ND','OH','OK','OR','PA','RI','SC',
    'SD','TN','TX','UT','VT','VA','WA','WV','WI','WY','DC','PR','GU','VI','AS','MP')),
  zip_code                varchar(10)  not null check (zip_code ~ '^[0-9]{5}(-[0-9]{4})?$'),
  insurance_provider      varchar(100),
  insurance_member_id     varchar(50)  check (insurance_member_id is null or insurance_member_id ~ '^[A-Za-z0-9]+$'),
  preferred_language      varchar(50)  not null default 'English',
  emergency_contact_name  varchar(100),
  emergency_contact_phone varchar(10)  check (emergency_contact_phone is null or emergency_contact_phone ~ '^[2-9][0-9]{2}[2-9][0-9]{6}$'),
  created_at              timestamptz  not null default now(),
  updated_at              timestamptz  not null default now(),
  deleted_at              timestamptz
);

-- Lookups used by API filters and duplicate detection; partial so soft-deleted rows don't count
create index if not exists idx_patients_phone     on patients (phone_number)      where deleted_at is null;
create index if not exists idx_patients_last_name on patients (lower(last_name))  where deleted_at is null;
create index if not exists idx_patients_dob       on patients (date_of_birth)     where deleted_at is null;

create or replace function set_updated_at() returns trigger as $$
begin new.updated_at = now(); return new; end;
$$ language plpgsql;

drop trigger if exists trg_patients_updated_at on patients;
create trigger trg_patients_updated_at before update on patients
  for each row execute function set_updated_at();

-- Bonus: appointments (mock single provider)
create table if not exists appointments (
  appointment_id uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  patient_id     uuid not null references patients(patient_id),
  scheduled_at   timestamptz not null,
  reason         varchar(200),
  status         varchar(20) not null default 'scheduled' check (status in ('scheduled', 'cancelled')),
  created_at     timestamptz not null default now()
);
create unique index if not exists uq_appointments_slot on appointments (scheduled_at) where status = 'scheduled';

-- Bonus: call logs / transcripts
create table if not exists call_logs (
  call_log_id       uuid primary key default gen_random_uuid(),
  vapi_call_id      varchar(100) not null unique,
  patient_id        uuid references patients(patient_id),
  caller_number     varchar(20),
  status            varchar(20) not null default 'in_progress' check (status in ('in_progress', 'completed', 'incomplete', 'failed')),
  ended_reason      varchar(100),
  summary           text,
  transcript        text,
  recording_url     text,
  collected_payload jsonb,
  started_at        timestamptz,
  ended_at          timestamptz,
  created_at        timestamptz not null default now(),
  updated_at        timestamptz not null default now()
);
drop trigger if exists trg_call_logs_updated_at on call_logs;
create trigger trg_call_logs_updated_at before update on call_logs
  for each row execute function set_updated_at();

-- Block Supabase's public REST API (anon key) from reading these tables.
-- Our backend connects as the table owner, so it is not affected.
alter table patients     enable row level security;
alter table appointments enable row level security;
alter table call_logs    enable row level security;
```
Note: `current_date` in a CHECK is allowed by Postgres and fine here because time only moves forward. The app layer does the timezone-aware check.

Seed (`supabase/seed.sql`): 1-2 obviously fake patients, e.g. Jane Doe, 555-01xx style numbers.

## Service layer rules
- `PatientService` methods: `create`, `get`, `list`, `update`, `soft_delete`, `find_active_by_phone`.
- All reads exclude `deleted_at is not null`.
- Wrap DB errors: integrity/check violations -> `ValidationFailed` with field info where possible; connection errors -> `DatabaseUnavailable`.
- `SIMULATE_DB_FAILURE` (only when APP_ENV=development) raises `DatabaseUnavailable` on writes, for testing scenario 15.
- Log `patient_created` / `patient_updated` with the final payload (brief requires it).

## Tests (`tests/`)
- `test_validators.py`: each normalizer/validator, including edge cases (leap day DOB, tomorrow's date, 11-digit phone with 1, ZIP+4 without dash, "texas" -> TX).
- `test_patients_api.py`: POST 201 + envelope, POST 422 details, malformed JSON 400, GET filters, GET 404, bad UUID 400, PUT partial, PUT empty 400, DELETE soft + second DELETE 404, deleted excluded from list.
- `test_tools.py`: tool dispatcher with both Vapi tool-call shapes, success / validation / server error results.
- `test_key_pool.py`: 429 rotates to next key and cools down, 401 disables key, all-fail returns fallback.
- Use a separate test database (TEST_DATABASE_URL) or dependency overrides. Never run tests against the live demo DB.
